  "post": {
    "title": "The 5 farthest things humans have ever built 🚀",
    "description": "Ranked by distance from Earth on 24 November 2026, computed with NASA/JPL Horizons:\n#5 New Horizons: about 10 billion km\n#4 Pioneer 11: 17.8 billion km\n#3 Pioneer 10: 21.2 billion km (launched 1972; the farthest until Voyager 1 caught it in 1998)\n#2 Voyager 2: 21.7 billion km\n#1 Voyager 1: 25.9 billion km, a full light-day away\n\nSources:\nNASA/JPL Horizons ephemeris service: https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/\nNASA Science, Pioneer 10 Sends Last Signal: https://science.nasa.gov/missions/pioneer/pioneer-10-sends-last-signal/\nNASA Science, Voyager 1: What Is a Light-Day: https://science.nasa.gov/mission/voyager/voyager-1/voyager-1-what-is-a-light-day/\n\nImages: NASA / JPL / MDSCC / INTA, Francisco \"Paco\" Moreno (Deep Space Network, Madrid), NASA / JPL (Voyager 2 launch), NASA / JPL / JPL-Caltech / KSC (Voyager 1 launch). Narration uses a synthetic voice.",
